          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On August 8, 2014, at midnight during a thunderstorm, a witness is intrigued by a luminous phenomenon in the clouds. The witness observes a white-blue glowing point that disappears and reappears a few meters further in the clouds. The witness's description of glowing points in a very cloudy and stormy sky (the witness describes at least one lightning flash) likely corresponds to a globular lightning phenomenon. The GEIPAN has not received the video mentioned by the witness and is unable to confirm the hypothesis, which remains highly probable. The GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable globular lightning.",
